meta {
  name: Smartscape Events Ingest default endpoint
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{DT_TENANT_URL}}/platform/ingest/v1/smartscape.events
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  [
    {
      "type": "SOME_TYPE",
      "id_components": [
        {
          "some": "id_input"
        },
        {
          "some_other": "other_id_input"
        }
      ],
      "timestamp": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "event.version": 1,
      "dt.security_context": "sensitive-data",
      "name": "smartscape node name",
      "ext.custom_property": "value",
      "tags:ext.my_source": {
        "key": "value",
        "otherKey": "otherValue"
      },
      "static_edges": {
        "belongs_to": [
          {
            "type": "SOME_OTHER_TYPE",
            "id_components": [
              {
                "another": "id_input"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  # Smartscape Events Ingest default endpoint

  The maximum payload size of a single request is **10 MiB**. Requests with a greater payload are rejected, and the API returns a 413 response code.

  <br />**Timestamp field**

  If there is no `timestamp` field in the request payload, the current server time is used as timestamp.

  If the `timestamp` field is present and it has a **numeric** value, the time unit is assumed based on the size of the value. Nano seconds by default.

  Afterwards, the field will be converted to a `Timestamp` type in nano seconds.

  If the `timestamp` field is present and has a string value, attempts are made to parse it based on UNIX epoch milliseconds or seconds, RFC3339 or RFC3164 format, in this order.

  If the `timestamp` has the wrong type (e.g. boolean, array) or cannot be properly parsed, it is overridden with the current server time and the original value is preserved.

  <br />**Smartscape event validation**

  Each event must identify an entity using exactly one of two modes:

  - **Mode 1** — supply a pre-computed `id` matching `[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*-[0-9A-F]{16}` (e.g. `HOST-0000000000000001`).
  - **Mode 2** — supply `type` (matching `[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*`) and `id_components` (a non-empty array of single-key objects whose values are strings). The two modes are mutually exclusive.

  - Structural keys (`type`, `id`, `id_components`, `dt.security_context`, `update_lifetime`, `timestamp`, `static_edges`, `dynamic_edges`, `event.version`) are reserved.
  - For core entity types (not `EXT_*` / `CUSTOM_*`), only `name`, `process.metadata[COMMAND_LINE_ARGS]`, and names starting with `ext.` or `custom.` are allowed.
  - Extended entity types (`EXT_*` / `CUSTOM_*`) bypass the allowlist (structural keys still reserved).
  - Field values must be scalar (string, number, boolean, or null) or a flat `string:string` object (both keys and values must be strings).

  **Tags** — tag contexts are top-level keys with a `tags:` prefix:

  - E.g. `"tags:ext.source": { "env": "production" }` defines a tag context `ext.source`.
  - For core entity types, context names (after stripping `tags:`) must start with `ext.` or `custom.`.
  - Extended entity types bypass this restriction.
  - Tag property values must be scalar (string, number, boolean, or null).

  **Schema versioning** — the optional `event.version` field (integer) declares which version of the smartscape event format your producer targets. Supplying it is strongly recommended: it guarantees a **stable interface** — if the format evolves under a new version, your events keep being processed exactly as before. Currently only version `1` is supported; unsupported values are rejected with a `400` response.

  Invalid events are rejected with a `400` response listing every offending field.

  **Auth:** OAuth (inherited from collection)

  **Required OAuth scopes:** `openpipeline:events.smartscape:ingest`

  **API token scopes:** openpipeline.events_smartscape
}
